        		<script language="javascript" type="text/javascript">
        	function checkChildren(srcObj, vType) {
        		for (var i = 0; i < eval("document.formSMC." + vType + ".length"); i++) {
        			if ((eval("document.formSMC." + vType + "[i].value.substring(0, srcObj.length)") == srcObj) && (eval("document.formSMC." + vType + "[i].disabled") == false)) {
        					(eval("document.formSMC." + vType + "[i].checked")) ? eval("document.formSMC." + vType + "[i]").checked = false : eval("document.formSMC." + vType + "[i]").checked = true;
        			}
        		}
        		return false;
        	}
        function toggleRepealed(element) {
        	const rows = document.getElementById("hideRepealed").querySelectorAll('tr');
        	rows.forEach(function (row) {
        		var text = row.textContent;		
        		if (text.includes('REPEALED') && !row.classList.contains('hidden')) {
        			row.classList.add('hidden')
        		}
        		else {
        			row.classList.remove('hidden')
        		}
        	})
        }
        function HideRepealed() {
        	const rows = document.getElementById("hideRepealed").querySelectorAll('tr');
        	rows.forEach(function (row) {
        		var text = row.textContent;		
        		if (text.includes('REPEALED') && !row.classList.contains('hidden')) {
        			row.classList.add('hidden')
        		}
        	})
        }
        </script>
        <div style="padding: 15px;"><form action="/smc/" method="post" name="formSMC">
        <div id="hideRepealed">
        		<p><a href="/smc/?Title=12">Title 12</a> Public Ways and Property</p>
        				<p><a href="/smc/?Chapter=12.01">Chapter 12.01</a> Improvement, Maintenance of Public Ways</p>
        					<a href="/smc/?Section=12.01.005">Section 12.01.005</a> Purpose<br />
        <p>The purpose of this title is to regulate and control the obstruction of public rights-of-way in the City so that those rights-of-way remain accessible and safe for their intended public use. No specific duty to particular persons is created hereby.</p>
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, June 25, 2007</p><p>Effective Date: Saturday, August 4, 2007</p><p>Recodification ORD C34053 Section 1</p>					<a href="/smc/?Section=12.01.010">Section 12.01.010</a> Sidewalk Maintenance – Owner’s Responsibility<br />
        <p style="margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify">&nbsp;</p>
        
        <ol style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">Every owner and occupant of premises shall keep the sidewalk area<u>,</u> including tree grates adjacent to any portion of the real property (including corners), in good and safe condition and repair at all times.</span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="2" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">Where the Director of Engineering Services determines there has been a failure to comply with this section, the Director or their designee may send written notice to the premises advising of the violation. If the violation is not corrected, the Director or their designee may proceed to remove or repair the condition, at the owner&rsquo;s and/or occupant&rsquo;s sole expense and liability.</span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="3" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">The Directors of Engineering Services, Development Services<u>,</u> Code Enforcement, and the City Engineer are authorized to&nbsp;waive license, bonding, and insurance requirements for minor repairs on existing sidewalks.</span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="4" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">The City Engineer, along with the Development Services and the Code Enforcement departments, shall develop and publish a public rule defining the types of sidewalk projects that qualify as minor repairs.</span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="5" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">Nothing in this section shall be construed to&nbsp;waive building and construction permit and inspection requirements.</span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <p style="margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify">&nbsp;</p>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, February 9, 2026</p><p>Effective Date: Thursday, March 19, 2026</p><p>ORD C36835 Section 8</p>					<a href="/smc/?Section=12.01.020">Section 12.01.020</a> REPEALED (Curb Barrier – Owner’s Responsibility)<br />
        <p>Repealed by ORD C33831.</p>
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, June 25, 2007</p><p>Effective Date: Saturday, August 4, 2007</p><p>Recodification ORD C34053 Section 1</p>					<a href="/smc/?Section=12.01.030">Section 12.01.030</a> REPEALED (Specifications, Surfaces)<br />
        <p>Repealed by ORD C33831.</p>
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, June 25, 2007</p><p>Effective Date: Saturday, August 4, 2007</p><p>Recodification ORD C34053 Section 1</p>					<a href="/smc/?Section=12.01.200">Section 12.01.200</a> REPEALED (Citizens Streets Advisory Commission (CSAC))<br />
        <p>REPEALED</p>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Thursday, November 14, 2024</p><p>Effective Date: Friday, December 20, 2024</p><p>ORD C36600 Section 1</p>						<p>Article I. Curbing, Sidewalks Required</p>
        							<a href="/smc/?Section=12.01.0402">Section 12.01.0402</a> REPEALED (Prohibitions – Exceptions)<br />
        <p>Repealed by ORD C33831.</p>
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, June 25, 2007</p><p>Effective Date: Saturday, August 4, 2007</p><p>Recodification ORD C34053 Section 1</p>							<a href="/smc/?Section=12.01.0404">Section 12.01.0404</a> REPEALED (Special Zones – Exceptions)<br />
        <p>Repealed by ORD C33831.</p>
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, June 25, 2007</p><p>Effective Date: Saturday, August 4, 2007</p><p>Recodification ORD C34053 Section 1</p>							<a href="/smc/?Section=12.01.0406">Section 12.01.0406</a> REPEALED (Arterial Paving)<br />
        <p>Repealed by ORD C33831.</p>
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, June 25, 2007</p><p>Effective Date: Saturday, August 4, 2007</p><p>Recodification ORD C34053 Section 1</p>							<a href="/smc/?Section=12.01.0408">Section 12.01.0408</a> REPEALED (Owner’s Obligation – Curbing, Sidewalk Exceptions)<br />
        <p>Repealed by ORD C33831.</p>
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, June 25, 2007</p><p>Effective Date: Saturday, August 4, 2007</p><p>Recodification ORD C34053 Section 1</p>							<a href="/smc/?Section=12.01.050">Section 12.01.050</a> REPEALED (Sidewalk Construction Policy)<br />
        <p>Repealed by ORD C33831.</p>
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, June 25, 2007</p><p>Effective Date: Saturday, August 4, 2007</p><p>Recodification ORD C34053 Section 1</p>						<p>Article II. Review for Sidewalks</p>
        							<a href="/smc/?Section=12.01.0602">Section 12.01.0602</a> REPEALED (Construction Approval)<br />
        <p>Repealed by ORD C33831.</p>
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, June 25, 2007</p><p>Effective Date: Saturday, August 4, 2007</p><p>Recodification ORD C34053 Section 1</p>							<a href="/smc/?Section=12.01.0606">Section 12.01.0606</a> REPEALED (Sidewalk Requirements – Exceptions)<br />
        <p>Repealed by ORD C33831.</p>
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, June 25, 2007</p><p>Effective Date: Saturday, August 4, 2007</p><p>Recodification ORD C34053 Section 1</p>							<a href="/smc/?Section=12.01.0608">Section 12.01.0608</a> REPEALED (Plenary Authority of Council)<br />
        <p>Repealed by ORD C33831.</p>
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, June 25, 2007</p><p>Effective Date: Saturday, August 4, 2007</p><p>Recodification ORD C34053 Section 1</p>							<a href="/smc/?Section=12.01.0610">Section 12.01.0610</a> REPEALED (Cost of Council-directed Improvements)<br />
        <p>Repealed by ORD C33831.</p>
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, June 25, 2007</p><p>Effective Date: Saturday, August 4, 2007</p><p>Recodification ORD C34053 Section 1</p>							<a href="/smc/?Section=12.01.0612">Section 12.01.0612</a> REPEALED (Time for Owner-constructed Improvement)<br />
        <p>Repealed by ORD C33831.</p>
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, June 25, 2007</p><p>Effective Date: Saturday, August 4, 2007</p><p>Recodification ORD C34053 Section 1</p>							<a href="/smc/?Section=12.01.070">Section 12.01.070</a> REPEALED (Curb Ramps for Sidewalks)<br />
        <p>Repealed by ORD C33831.</p>
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, June 25, 2007</p><p>Effective Date: Saturday, August 4, 2007</p><p>Recodification ORD C34053 Section 1</p>						<p>Article III. Pedestrian Strip</p>
        							<a href="/smc/?Section=12.01.0802">Section 12.01.0802</a> REPEALED (New Construction – Obligations)<br />
        <p>Repealed by ORD C33831.</p>
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, June 25, 2007</p><p>Effective Date: Saturday, August 4, 2007</p><p>Recodification ORD C34053 Section 1</p>							<a href="/smc/?Section=12.01.0804">Section 12.01.0804</a> Pedestrian Strip – All Streets – Obligations<br />
        <ol style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align: justify;">On streets where no formally constructed sidewalk exists for pedestrian traffic, the abutting property owner shall maintain a strip of land for pedestrian travel in the existing public right-of-way area adjacent to the constructed street or roadway. This strip of land shall run parallel to and abut the constructed street or roadway. It shall be seven feet wide, but not greater than the publically dedicated or reserved outer boundaries of the right of way as shown in the plat or other records. This strip shall contain no fences, shrubs, walls or any other feature that would prohibit, inhibit or impede pedestrian travel. [Cross Reference: <a href="http://my.spokanecity.org/smc/?Section=16A.61.570">SMC 16A.61.570</a>]<br />
        	&nbsp;</li>
        	<li style="text-align: justify;">The City recognizes its right to enforce public use of said right-of-way for pedestrian travel and the city council may, upon recommendation from the City plan commission or City staff, in addition to or in the alternative to other lawful procedures, order the property owners who abut any certain street or streets within the city to maintain an unobstructed strip of land as provided herein when it is determined by the city council to be necessary to the health and safety of the citizens of Spokane.</li>
        </ol>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, January 10, 2011</p><p>Effective Date: Thursday, February 17, 2011</p><p>ORD C34684 Section 1</p>							<a href="/smc/?Section=12.01.090">Section 12.01.090</a> REPEALED (Variances)<br />
        <p>Repealed by ORD C33831.</p>
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, June 25, 2007</p><p>Effective Date: Saturday, August 4, 2007</p><p>Recodification ORD C34053 Section 1</p>						<p>Article IV. Commercial Driveways</p>
        							<a href="/smc/?Section=12.01.1202">Section 12.01.1202</a> REPEALED (Policy)<br />
        <p>Repealed by ORD C33831.</p>
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, June 25, 2007</p><p>Effective Date: Saturday, August 4, 2007</p><p>Recodification ORD C34053 Section 1</p>							<a href="/smc/?Section=12.01.1204">Section 12.01.1204</a> REPEALED (Commercial Driveway Defined)<br />
        <p>Repealed by ORD C33831.</p>
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, June 25, 2007</p><p>Effective Date: Saturday, August 4, 2007</p><p>Recodification ORD C34053 Section 1</p>							<a href="/smc/?Section=12.01.1206">Section 12.01.1206</a> REPEALED (Commercial Driveway – Width – Spacing)<br />
        <p>Repealed by ORD C33831.</p>
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, June 25, 2007</p><p>Effective Date: Saturday, August 4, 2007</p><p>Recodification ORD C34053 Section 1</p>							<a href="/smc/?Section=12.01.1208">Section 12.01.1208</a> REPEALED (Commercial Driveway – Total Width – Frontage)<br />
        <p>Repealed by ORD C33831.</p>
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, June 25, 2007</p><p>Effective Date: Saturday, August 4, 2007</p><p>Recodification ORD C34053 Section 1</p>							<a href="/smc/?Section=12.01.1210">Section 12.01.1210</a> REPEALED (Commercial Driveways – Spacing per Ownership/Leasehold)<br />
        <p>Repealed by ORD C33831.</p>
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, June 25, 2007</p><p>Effective Date: Saturday, August 4, 2007</p><p>Recodification ORD C34053 Section 1</p>							<a href="/smc/?Section=12.01.1212">Section 12.01.1212</a> REPEALED (Variances – Approval)<br />
        <p>Repealed by ORD C33831.</p>
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, June 25, 2007</p><p>Effective Date: Saturday, August 4, 2007</p><p>Recodification ORD C34053 Section 1</p>							<a href="/smc/?Section=12.01.1214">Section 12.01.1214</a> REPEALED (Regulations – Plans)<br />
        <p>Repealed by ORD C33831.</p>
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, June 25, 2007</p><p>Effective Date: Saturday, August 4, 2007</p><p>Recodification ORD C34053 Section 1</p>						<p>Article V. Sidewalk Relocation – Damage</p>
        							<a href="/smc/?Section=12.01.1302">Section 12.01.1302</a> Prohibitions – “Public Sidewalk” Defined<br />
        <p>
        <ol type="A">
        <li>No person may relocate or change the grade or other aspects of the public sidewalk without permission from the director of engineering services, and only upon such conditions as he or she may require.<br />&nbsp;</li>
        <li>“Public sidewalk” refers to all pedestrian lanes, walkways, or areas of public passage or commerce used primarily for foot traffic and publicly dedicated or reserved for said purpose. Nothing herein shall affect the authority of the park board to regulate areas under its jurisdiction. </li></ol>
        <p></p>
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, June 25, 2007</p><p>Effective Date: Saturday, August 4, 2007</p><p>Recodification ORD C34053 Section 1</p>							<a href="/smc/?Section=12.01.1304">Section 12.01.1304</a> Sidewalk Relocation Permit<br />
        <p>Applications to relocate or change a sidewalk shall be submitted to the director of engineering services by the owner of the property abutting the same. Said applications shall contain such information as the director requires.</p>
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, June 25, 2007</p><p>Effective Date: Saturday, August 4, 2007</p><p>Recodification ORD C34053 Section 1</p>							<a href="/smc/?Section=12.01.1306">Section 12.01.1306</a> Damage, Disturbance Forbidden<br />
        <p>No person shall by any means, including heat, compression, under-mining, vibration, or direct or indirect invasion, damage or disturb any public pavement, street, alley, or sidewalk, or cause or allow others to cause damage or destruction of the same by any means, whether direct or indirect. This includes sudden or gradual invasions.</p>
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, June 25, 2007</p><p>Effective Date: Saturday, August 4, 2007</p><p>Recodification ORD C34053 Section 1</p>						<p>Article VI. Railroads – Paving Right-of-way</p>
        							<a href="/smc/?Section=12.01.1402">Section 12.01.1402</a> Policy<br />
        <p>The city council finds it is in the public interest, health, and safety to require all railroads to pave portions of their rights-of-way crossings at any paved street or alley.</p>
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, June 25, 2007</p><p>Effective Date: Saturday, August 4, 2007</p><p>Recodification ORD C34053 Section 1</p>							<a href="/smc/?Section=12.01.1404">Section 12.01.1404</a> Railroad Shall Pave Crossings<br />
        <p>
        <ol type="A">
        <li>Whenever any railroad shall cross at grade any paved surface, street, sidewalk, or alley (paved area), the railroad or owner of the right-of-way crossing must pave at its own expense and to the satisfaction and approval of the director of engineering services, the entire right-of-way crossing lying within said paved area, and thereafter maintain the same.<br />&nbsp;</li>
        <li>Specifications and regulations for such paving shall be provided by the director of engineering services. </li></ol>
        <p></p>
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, June 25, 2007</p><p>Effective Date: Saturday, August 4, 2007</p><p>Recodification ORD C34053 Section 1</p>							<a href="/smc/?Section=12.01.150">Section 12.01.150</a> Public Service Corporations – Notice<br />
        <ol style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align: justify;">Where the City orders improvements of any area of the public right-of-way for which municipal franchise privileges have been extended to a public service corporation, or otherwise where the director of engineering services deems appropriate, the director requires persons performing such improvements to notify the affected companies by use of the one-call system and/or by such written notification as the director may establish. The one-call system is a procedure of telephone notification supported by the industry and existing in Spokane.<br />
        	&nbsp;</li>
        	<li style="text-align: justify;">Subject to any express reservations in municipal franchises or applicable laws, the notification given shall advise the affected public service corporations to make such changes in their use or occupancy of the public right-of-way as may be deemed necessary by the director of engineering services to accommodate the improvement. Such changes shall be at the sole expense and liability of the affected public service company and no charge, cost, or liability shall accrue to the City, its agents or contractors for said changes.<br />
        	&nbsp;</li>
        	<li style="text-align: justify;">The notice shall specify the time for such changes to be accomplished, and if the required changes are not timely made, the company or contractor responsible for the improvement may be instructed by the director of engineering services to proceed to make such necessary changes or accommodation in any property or fixture of the public service corporation. Such changes are at the public service corporation&rsquo;s sole expense and liability, in addition to any penalties imposed for violation of this title.</li>
        </ol>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, June 25, 2007</p><p>Effective Date: Saturday, August 4, 2007</p><p>Recodification ORD C34053 Section 1</p>						<p>Article VII. Citizens Streets Advisory Commission</p>
        							<a href="/smc/?Section=12.01.205">Section 12.01.205</a> REPEALED (Procedures and Internal Operations)<br />
        <p>REPEALED</p>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Thursday, November 14, 2024</p><p>Effective Date: Friday, December 20, 2024</p><p>ORD C36600 Section 1</p>							<a href="/smc/?Section=12.01.210">Section 12.01.210</a> REPEALED (Functions, Powers and Duties)<br />
        <p>REPEALED</p>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Thursday, November 14, 2024</p><p>Effective Date: Friday, December 20, 2024</p><p>ORD C36600 Section 1</p>				<p><a href="/smc/?Chapter=12.02">Chapter 12.02</a> Obstruction, Encroachment of Public Ways</p>
        					<a href="/smc/?Section=12.02.005">Section 12.02.005</a> Purpose<br />
        <p>The purpose of this chapter is to regulate and control the obstruction of public rights-of-way in the City so that those rights-of-way remain accessible and safe for their intended public use. No specific duty to particular persons is created hereby.</p>
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, June 25, 2007</p><p>Effective Date: Saturday, August 4, 2007</p><p>Recodification ORD C34053 Section 1</p>					<a href="/smc/?Section=12.02.010">Section 12.02.010</a> Snow Removal – Owner, Occupant Duties<br />
        <ol style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">Owners and occupants of premises shall keep the sidewalk areas adjacent to any portion of the real property (including corners) free and clear of snow and/or accumulations of snow or ice.</span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="2" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">No snow or ice from private premises shall be plowed into or placed in or on the streets or other areas of the public right of way, parks or other public property. This does not apply to operations by municipal crews. Snow or ice from sidewalks and driveway approaches may be placed in planting strips, or added to berms created by municipal plowing operations, provided it does not obstruct a clear view of stop signs or other traffic signs or signals, other otherwise create a hazard to or impairment of pedestrian or vehicular traffic. This section applies to:</span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol>
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">homeowners of single family residences, duplexes or triplexes;</span></span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="2">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">by persons in business of plowing or clearing snow; and</span></span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="3">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">anyone other than parties noted in (B)(1) or (B)(2), such as business, commercial, multiunit premises, etc;</span></span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, February 13, 2012</p><p>Effective Date: Saturday, March 24, 2012</p><p>ORD C34832 Section 1</p>					<a href="/smc/?Section=12.02.060">Section 12.02.060</a> Fences and Hedges – Incidental Encroachments<br />
        <p style="margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify">&nbsp;</p>
        
        <p style="margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Aptos,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">Incidental encroachments&nbsp;upon the public right-of-way from private property not obstructing the use of the right-of-way may be permitted by the Director of Development Services or their designee as provided in&nbsp;</span><a href="https://my.spokanecity.org/smc/?Section=17G.010.160" style="color:blue; text-decoration:underline" target="_blank">SMC 17G.010.160</a><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">. Such encroachments&nbsp;are revocable without compensation and create no vested rights.</span></span></p>
        
        <p style="margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify">&nbsp;</p>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, October 20, 2025</p><p>Effective Date: Friday, November 28, 2025</p><p>ORD C36753 Section 6</p>					<a href="/smc/?Section=12.02.902">Section 12.02.902</a> REPEALED<br />
