        <p>Date Passed: Monday, October 27, 2025</p><p>Effective Date: Monday, October 27, 2025</p><p>ORD C36785 Section 3</p>							<a href="/smc/?Section=12.02.1002">Section 12.02.1002</a> REPEALED (Definitions)<br />
        <p>REPEALED&nbsp;</p>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, June 30, 2025</p><p>Effective Date: Wednesday, August 6, 2025</p><p>ORD C36679 Section 4</p>							<a href="/smc/?Section=12.02.1003">Section 12.02.1003</a> Protection Against Harm to Waterways<br />
        <p style="margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify">&nbsp;</p>
        
        <ol style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">No person may cause harm to the Spokane River or Latah Creek or to the banks and natural areas that buffer these waterways. No person may do any of the following:</span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol>
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">Build or erect a structure of any type along the Spokane River or Latah Creek, or drive a nail or other object into any tree or other natural vegetation for the purpose of building a shelter or any other structure, or for affixing an object to any tree or other natural vegetation.</span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="2">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">Dig on the banks of the Spokane River or Latah Creek.</span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="3">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">Move boulders, destroy vegetation, pave roads or paths, or otherwise reconfigure the natural landscape or other City-approved development on the banks of the Spokane River or Latah Creek.</span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="4">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">Drive, park<u>,</u> or bring any vehicle onto any portion of the banks of the Spokane River or Latah Creek.</span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="5">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">Discharge garbage, refuse, or human or animal waste along the banks or into the waters of the Spokane River or Latah Creek.</span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="2" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">Any violation of this section shall be punishable as a misdemeanor.</span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="3" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">In addition to prosecution of a violation under this section, where conduct constitutes an unpermitted or unlawful discharge or pollution event under RCW 90.48, the City may also refer the matter to the Washington State Department of Ecology for enforcement under state law, or where conduct constitutes a shoreline violation under RCW 90.58, the City may enforce under its Shoreline Master Program SMC 17E.060 or refer to the Department of Ecology as appropriate.</span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <p style="margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify">&nbsp;</p>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, October 27, 2025</p><p>Effective Date: Monday, October 27, 2025</p><p>ORD C36785 Section 4</p>							<a href="/smc/?Section=12.02.1004">Section 12.02.1004</a> Injury to Tree on Public Property - Violation<br />
        <p style="margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify">&nbsp;</p>
        
        <p style="margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">No person may destroy, injure, or deface any street tree or public tree on public property by any means, as provided in SMC 12.02.970.</span></span></p>
        
        <p style="margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify">&nbsp;</p>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, October 27, 2025</p><p>Effective Date: Monday, October 27, 2025</p><p>ORD C36785 Section 5</p></form>
        </div>
        </div></td>
        	</tr>
        </table>
